			<p>We are a country and a world divided more than ever before. Our collective situation has been compared to many embattled periods of conflict in history but…</p>
			<blockquote>Never before in this country have we experienced a total loss of agreement on how to perceive reality or information itself.</blockquote>
		</div>
		<div id="fighting-2">
			<p>This is not surprising because all new war tactics are unfamiliar to the first generation of victims they are used on. As a whole, we are untrained on the rules of information warfare, which is a war fought in the background, by obfuscated entities, on a public that is unaware of its participation.</p>
			<p>This is the world we live in today, and the only way to fight information warfare is to know better, to understand the rules of war by studying the tactics, to ask questions, and to always remember that the truth will stand up to scrutiny. The abilities to think, to be mindful, to be analytical, and to be observant are now valuable defenses in this war.</p>
